-- title:
--   Hartogs for R₂-integral functions integral over ℚ̄[j]
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a positive integer $N$, an algebraically closed field $k$ of characteristic $q$ and a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$; fix modular polynomial data `data` for $q$ satisfying the Kronecker congruence $\Phi \equiv (CX^{q} - X)(CX - X^{q}) \bmod q$, integrality hypotheses $h\alpha$, $h\beta$ for the two degeneracy maps from level $N$ to level $Nq$ on the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base-changed modular function fields, and a specialisation packet $P$ of type `PlaceSpecialization` for these data. Assume $q \nmid N$, let $R$ be a `ProlongationTuple` over $P$, and let $Q$ be a place of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ inside the level-$Nq$ field `modularFunctionFieldBar (N * q)` which is strict of the second kind for $P$, i.e. $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\,Q$ is the Frobenius image of $\bar v := P.\mathrm{reduceSnd}\,Q$ while the twofold Frobenius image of $\bar v$ differs from $\bar v$. Assume there is $c \in k \times k$ whose two coordinates are centres of $\bar v$, in the sense that $\bar v$ gives positive order to $j_{\mathrm{geom}} - c_1$ and to $j_{N,\mathrm{geom}} - c_2$ in `modularFunctionFieldC k N`, and that $\bar v$ is the only place of that field with this property; assume also that the values of $j_{\mathrm{geom}}$ and of $j_{N,\mathrm{geom}}$ at $\bar v$ are both moved by $x \mapsto x^{q^{2}}$. Let $z, y_1, y_2$ lie in `modularFunctionFieldBar (N * q)`, let $u \in A$ and $w : \mathrm{Fin}\,2 \to A$, and suppose $(\bar v, \mathrm{red}\,u, z, y_1, y_2)$ is a second-kind triple: either $z = j(\mathfrak q^{q})$, $y_1 = j(\mathfrak q^{Nq})$, $y_2 = j$ with $\mathrm{ord}_{\bar v}(j_{\mathrm{geom}} - \mathrm{red}\,u) = 1$, or $z = j(\mathfrak q^{Nq})$, $y_1 = j(\mathfrak q^{q})$, $y_2 = j$ with $\mathrm{ord}_{\bar v}(j_{N,\mathrm{geom}} - \mathrm{red}\,u) = 1$; suppose moreover $Q$ gives positive order to $z - u$ and to $y_j - w_j$ for $j = 0, 1$. Then for every $g$ in the valuation subring $R.R_2.\mathrm{integers}$ of the second regular prolongation which is integral over the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subalgebra generated by $j$, there exist polynomials $p, s$ over $A$ in three variables indexed by $\mathrm{Option}(\mathrm{Fin}\,2)$ such that, evaluating through $A \to \overline{\mathbb Q} \to$ `modularFunctionFieldBar (N * q)` at $(z; y_1, y_2)$, one has $p(z, y_1, y_2) = g \cdot s(z, y_1, y_2)$, while $\mathrm{red}\bigl(s(u, w_0, w_1)\bigr) \neq 0$.
--
--   This is the second-kind analogue of the statement that a function on the three-coordinate model of $X_0(Nq)$ which is regular for the second Gauss prolongation and integral over $\overline{\mathbb Q}[j]$ is a ratio of polynomials in the three coordinates whose denominator does not reduce to zero at the chosen point, a normality (Hartogs-type) step in the analysis of the mod-$q$ fibre at a supersingular-free point. It feeds the model-building statement [`ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.ProlongationTuple.IsModel.exists_evalBar_eq_mul_evalBar_of_mem_smoothLocalRingSnd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.ProlongationTuple.IsModel.exists_evalBar_eq_mul_evalBar_of_mem_smoothLocalRingSnd).
